WEBVTT

00:00:06.130 --> 00:00:07.600
Michiyo! Matsutaro!

00:00:08.090 --> 00:00:10.600
Did you bring something to give Gucchi,
 since he's moving away?

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:11.740
Yup.

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:12.150
<b>Sankyu</b>

00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:13.960
It's a ramen spoon!

00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:15.400
It's from Sankyu-san!

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:16.610
That's super rare!

00:00:16.610 --> 00:00:18.950
I brought you a sparkly box!

00:00:18.950 --> 00:00:22.500
I bought the supplies to make it at a 
100-yen shop with my mom and made it.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:24.300
There's a diamond stuck on there!

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:25.870
Wow.

00:00:25.870 --> 00:00:27.620
What's your present, Chuta?

00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:29.660
Dolls of us.

00:00:29.660 --> 00:00:31.100
Wow!

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:33.960
Did you sew those, Chuta? 
You're better than my mom!

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:38.220
I didn't sew them, I knitted them. 
They're called amigurumi.

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:39.800
The pink one must be me.

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:41.230
The red one is me.

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:43.960
That doesn't really look like me...

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:45.840
Aren't these great, Gucchi?

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:48.140
Yeah! Thanks, everyone!

00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:52.320
So, uh... This is hard for me to say...

00:00:53.050 --> 00:00:55.180
I'm not moving away anymore.

00:00:56.970 --> 00:00:58.230
Huh?

00:00:58.230 --> 00:00:59.460
What?

00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:01.020
Huh?!

00:01:01.020 --> 00:01:06.570
My mom knew how much I would miss you guys, 
so my mom talked to my dad,

00:01:06.570 --> 00:01:08.660
and I won't be moving this year.

00:01:08.660 --> 00:01:10.810
Why didn't you tell us sooner?

00:01:10.810 --> 00:01:12.880
Then could I have that spoon back?

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:15.670
Then I want to use that 
sparkly box myself, too.

00:01:15.670 --> 00:01:18.610
Huh? Hey, that's not fair!

00:01:18.610 --> 00:01:21.280
You guys gave me these because 
you care about me, right?

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:24.400
Then why don't we make a time capsule?

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:28.950
We'll put everything in Michiyo's box, and then 
we'll open it years or even decades later.

00:01:28.950 --> 00:01:30.810
Decades...

00:01:30.810 --> 00:01:33.010
That's really exciting.

00:01:33.010 --> 00:01:36.320
It'll belong to everyone, so that means 
it'll be yours, too, Gucchi.

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:38.630
Yeah, but...

00:01:38.630 --> 00:01:41.110
Then Gucchi needs something to bury, too.

00:01:41.110 --> 00:01:45.150
Me? That's pretty sudden...

00:01:45.730 --> 00:01:46.910
Oh, yeah.

00:01:47.590 --> 00:01:51.290
My mom told me to give you guys this picture 
that she took of us before.

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:53.420
That's perfect!

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:57.560
All right, done. Let's go bury it.

00:03:28.970 --> 00:03:32.230
<b>A Pursuer From the Past: Part 1</b>

00:03:32.050 --> 00:03:33.100
It's no use.

00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:34.810
It's not here!

00:03:34.810 --> 00:03:39.340
You really don't remember where we 
buried the time capsule, Dolugh?

00:03:39.340 --> 00:03:41.340
I was asleep at the time.

00:03:42.520 --> 00:03:45.020
I'm pretty sure it's somewhere around here...

00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:47.960
You've changed recently, Chuta.

00:03:47.960 --> 00:03:52.080
You're actually talking about the three 
who got lost and disappeared.

00:03:53.080 --> 00:03:56.710
It might be because I joined ēlDLIVE 
and a lot's happened.

00:03:57.320 --> 00:04:00.480
I just realized that I can't 
keep running forever.

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:02.130
<b>Grade School Students Go Missing</b>

00:04:02.130 --> 00:04:03.300
<b>Likelihood of Survival: Low</b>

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:05.470
<b>Mudslide Occurs on Mount Taketori 
During Outing</b>

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:05.470
<b>Investigations 
Continue With 
No Luck</b>

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:10.770
Help me!

00:04:10.770 --> 00:04:11.840
Chuta!

00:04:11.840 --> 00:04:14.560
Wait right there! I'll save you!

00:04:15.110 --> 00:04:16.150
Okay...

00:04:16.870 --> 00:04:18.610
Chuta, the rock on the right...

00:04:18.610 --> 00:04:19.520
The right? Got it!

00:04:19.520 --> 00:04:21.100
No, that one's dangerous!

00:04:22.890 --> 00:04:26.470
Chuta!

00:04:27.350 --> 00:04:33.900
Isn't it ironic? No matter how much I tried 
to run away from my past, I couldn't.

00:04:33.900 --> 00:04:37.310
And now that I'm trying to get 
closer to it, it's gone.

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:44.340
<b>Mizoguchi 
Family Grave</b>

00:04:39.890 --> 00:04:43.620
It's been a while since you've 
been to Gucchi's grave, Chuta.

00:04:43.620 --> 00:04:44.340
Yeah.

00:04:44.770 --> 00:04:46.640
It's a bit early,

00:04:47.130 --> 00:04:50.750
but it'd be awkward to run into 
Gucchi's mom and the others.

00:04:52.730 --> 00:04:55.350
Why were you the only one to survive?!

00:04:55.350 --> 00:04:58.330
Why are you still here when Ken's gone?!

00:04:58.970 --> 00:05:02.840
That was the first time someone 
ever glared at me like that.

00:05:04.770 --> 00:05:06.350
But it can't be helped.

00:05:06.970 --> 00:05:08.950
It's all my fault.

00:05:10.070 --> 00:05:13.530
After that, Mimi held you and 
she bawled her eyes out.

00:05:13.530 --> 00:05:17.770
Huh? Aunt Mimi did? 
Did that actually happen?

00:05:17.770 --> 00:05:20.470
Well, you were completely in shock.

00:05:20.940 --> 00:05:23.540
Oh... I guess I sort of 
remember that, after all.

00:05:24.740 --> 00:05:29.680
Aunt Mimi was crying... 
and held my back tight.

00:05:30.590 --> 00:05:32.380
For three months after that day,

00:05:32.380 --> 00:05:35.840
Mimi was crying in her futon 
after you fell asleep.

00:05:35.840 --> 00:05:37.520
S-Seriously?

00:05:38.450 --> 00:05:41.590
<i>I was so worried about myself...</i>

00:05:42.100 --> 00:05:46.540
<i>Auntie must have gone through 
a lot because of me...</i>

00:05:48.900 --> 00:05:52.620
And so, I hope you all 
greet each other this month

00:05:52.620 --> 00:05:54.520
as energetic Shirobori Middle School 
students should.

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:56.160
This is boring, isn't it, Chuta?

00:05:56.160 --> 00:05:59.360
Next, in regards to interactions 
with the community...

00:05:58.860 --> 00:06:03.180
<i>Crap... If I actually fall asleep, 
Sonokata's gonna bug me again...</i>

00:06:03.580 --> 00:06:04.700
<i>Huh?</i>

00:06:05.910 --> 00:06:08.460
Sensei! Sonokata-san passed out!

00:06:09.270 --> 00:06:10.470
What happened?

00:06:11.120 --> 00:06:12.810
Something smells...

00:06:13.750 --> 00:06:15.590
D-Dolugh?

00:06:16.490 --> 00:06:17.840
What's wrong, Chuta?

00:06:18.610 --> 00:06:20.810
N-Nothing. I'm just talking 
to myself, as usual.

00:06:22.210 --> 00:06:25.390
<i>Oh, yeah. I forgot to put 
on my headphone patch.</i>

00:06:26.050 --> 00:06:28.020
This is Inspector Chips, chu.

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:31.770
I declare Misuzu and Dolugh 
fainting an emergency,

00:06:31.770 --> 00:06:33.440
and will go retrieve them now, chu.

00:06:33.760 --> 00:06:34.690
Retrieve?

00:06:49.770 --> 00:06:54.850
I'm Sonokata's mother, chu... 
I mean, I'm her mother.

00:06:55.260 --> 00:06:57.080
That's Misuzu's mom?

00:06:57.080 --> 00:06:58.960
What? They don't look alike at all.

00:06:59.970 --> 00:07:04.510
I just happened to be passing by, chu... 
I mean, I just happened to be passing by.

00:07:05.010 --> 00:07:08.280
There's no doubt about it. 
That's Inspector Chips.

00:07:08.720 --> 00:07:13.110
The only humanoid robot that was immediately 
available was this Melpleian one, chu.

00:07:15.510 --> 00:07:21.250
Misuzu hasn't been feeling well all morning, 
so I'll take her home now, chu... Yes.

00:07:21.250 --> 00:07:25.990
Yamanaka-kun, is that really her mother?

00:07:25.990 --> 00:07:29.880
It's strange, but I can't seem 
to remember for sure...

00:07:33.490 --> 00:07:35.590
Misuzu, it's me.

00:07:36.770 --> 00:07:39.050
Oh... Mom.

00:07:39.050 --> 00:07:41.870
She said "Mom." Which means...

00:07:41.870 --> 00:07:44.430
...that person really is her mom?

00:07:49.020 --> 00:07:54.020
Um... Ma'am. We can't really 
have you just take your daughter...

00:07:56.600 --> 00:07:57.860
She's ill.

00:07:59.950 --> 00:08:05.360
Oh, and coincidentally, I received word 
from Chuta Kokonose's aunt,

00:08:05.360 --> 00:08:09.040
and for various reasons, 
she wants him to come home, chu.

00:08:09.040 --> 00:08:09.960
Huh?

00:08:09.960 --> 00:08:11.430
Hurry up and come with me, chu.

00:08:11.430 --> 00:08:14.070
Yoyo... I mean, right!

00:08:18.830 --> 00:08:21.790
Does that mean their parents 
know about their relationship?

00:08:21.790 --> 00:08:24.260
That's so nice. I'm sort of jealous.

00:08:25.210 --> 00:08:26.770
We were able to smoke them out.

00:08:26.770 --> 00:08:29.430
So it's Misuzu Sonokata...

00:08:29.940 --> 00:08:31.980
...and Chuta Kokonose from Class 2-A.

00:08:34.890 --> 00:08:38.240
Looks like you haven't been 
infected by any bacteria.

00:08:38.240 --> 00:08:41.580
Then the only reason I can think of

00:08:41.580 --> 00:08:45.970
is an SPH that induces sleep.

00:08:45.970 --> 00:08:51.090
Um, how long do I need to stay like this?

00:08:51.090 --> 00:08:53.340
I don't like this water. It's gross.

00:08:53.950 --> 00:08:58.950
The personnel that fainted 
could have been exposed,

00:08:58.950 --> 00:09:03.340
so I have to replace the fluids 
within your body as well as Misuzu's.

00:09:03.340 --> 00:09:03.970
Huh?!

00:09:03.970 --> 00:09:07.120
S-Sonokata's naked, too?

00:09:07.570 --> 00:09:10.230
Wh-Wh-Wh-Where is she?! Is she visible?!

00:09:10.230 --> 00:09:13.740
These tanks are made with two-way mirrors 
and can't be seen from the outside.

00:09:13.740 --> 00:09:16.330
Oh... I see.

00:09:16.330 --> 00:09:19.240
Also, the mics are on in all of the tanks.

00:09:19.240 --> 00:09:20.570
Huh?

00:09:21.250 --> 00:09:23.070
You pervert.

00:09:23.650 --> 00:09:26.950
Disappear. Disappear.

00:09:26.950 --> 00:09:29.870
Aaaah! She heard me!

00:09:27.560 --> 00:09:29.870
You can hear her clear as a bell.

00:09:31.370 --> 00:09:33.940
In regards to the incident of 
Misuzu and Dolugh fainting,

00:09:33.940 --> 00:09:35.620
both the suspect and the
 motive are unknown.

00:09:36.600 --> 00:09:40.140
That goes for the sleep-inducing SPH 
we believed that was used, as well.

00:09:40.140 --> 00:09:44.050
Yes, the SPH radar did not detect anything.

00:09:44.050 --> 00:09:46.920
But Dolugh mentioned that 
he smelled something.

00:09:46.920 --> 00:09:48.830
I didn't smell anything.

00:09:48.830 --> 00:09:51.910
The ability to sense SPH is 
different with every individual,

00:09:51.910 --> 00:09:54.060
so it's possible that both 
of you would not sense it.

00:09:54.060 --> 00:09:58.440
But it's strange that the SPH radar 
didn't detect anything.

00:09:58.440 --> 00:10:00.910
Anyway, we checked for suspicious individuals

00:10:00.910 --> 00:10:03.800
and anything that changed at the
 school between yesterday and today.

00:10:03.800 --> 00:10:06.370
There were two transfer students, 
a first-year and a third-year.

00:10:06.840 --> 00:10:07.910
Transfer students?

00:10:08.980 --> 00:10:10.580
Do these two look familiar?

00:10:10.580 --> 00:10:11.860
No.

00:10:11.860 --> 00:10:13.080
They do not.

00:10:13.080 --> 00:10:14.210
I see...

00:10:14.210 --> 00:10:17.220
However, that's the only clue we have.

00:10:17.220 --> 00:10:19.160
Keep an eye on them starting tomorrow.

00:10:19.160 --> 00:10:20.580
Yoyosa!

00:10:20.960 --> 00:10:22.650
It might be mere consolation,

00:10:22.650 --> 00:10:27.090
but take this awakening medicine, 
which should work against any sleep-inducing SPH.

00:10:27.090 --> 00:10:29.480
Take it before they try 
to put you to sleep.

00:10:29.790 --> 00:10:31.650
One more thing.

00:10:31.650 --> 00:10:35.520
We've just received word that a ship 
from the giant criminal organization DeMille

00:10:35.520 --> 00:10:37.640
is heading toward this solar system.

00:10:38.470 --> 00:10:42.200
DeMille is the criminal organization 
that you mentioned, right?

00:10:44.160 --> 00:10:45.730
DeMille is heading to Earth?

00:10:47.500 --> 00:10:49.200
You ready, chu?

00:10:49.200 --> 00:10:50.830
Yoyosa!

00:10:50.830 --> 00:10:54.050
Why do we have to conduct 
this training right now?

00:10:54.050 --> 00:10:56.590
It was requested by Officer Kokonose, chu.

00:10:57.130 --> 00:11:02.260
DeMille may have been involved in the 
incident today, so I wanted to train just in case.

00:11:02.260 --> 00:11:03.750
I believe that this is futile.

00:11:04.900 --> 00:11:09.980
Looks like Misuzu is still mad because 
you tried to see her naked, Chuta.

00:11:09.980 --> 00:11:15.300
Sonokata, sorry about earlier. 
The whole naked... I mean, the tank thing.

00:11:15.300 --> 00:11:16.870
I'm not worried about it.

00:11:17.610 --> 00:11:20.770
She says that, but she's 
more distant than usual.

00:11:20.770 --> 00:11:22.140
Yeah...

00:11:22.990 --> 00:11:28.250
After you input the difficulty level on that panel,
 targets will come out from that pot,

00:11:28.250 --> 00:11:30.910
and you'll have to fight them using 
various SPH techniques, chu.

00:11:30.910 --> 00:11:32.660
First, Officer Kokonose.

00:11:33.490 --> 00:11:34.660
Yoyosa!

00:11:35.140 --> 00:11:36.500
Level 1, chu.

00:11:39.340 --> 00:11:40.730
Something small is heading toward me!

00:11:40.730 --> 00:11:42.210
They look like flies, Chuta.

00:11:42.210 --> 00:11:44.900
If the targets come in contact with you, 
you'll swell up, chu.

00:11:44.900 --> 00:11:47.460
Just like getting stung by a bee on Earth.

00:11:47.460 --> 00:11:51.090
What? You should've told me that earlier! 
S-Sew them up, Dolugh!

00:11:51.600 --> 00:11:52.930
Sympathy!

00:11:56.150 --> 00:11:57.790
Oh, we got them.

00:11:57.790 --> 00:11:59.270
Barely.

00:11:59.270 --> 00:12:02.000
It's your turn next, Officer Sonokata.

00:12:02.000 --> 00:12:04.440
I'd like level 20, please.

00:12:04.440 --> 00:12:06.780
Huh? Level 20?!

00:12:29.160 --> 00:12:32.070
<i>I'm left in awe again...</i>

00:12:32.510 --> 00:12:34.640
Impressive as usual, Misuzu.

00:12:35.020 --> 00:12:38.440
Unlike Dr. Isaac, who looks over the 
wellbeing of all of the personnel,

00:12:38.440 --> 00:12:41.250
or Tonto-san, who manages the ship,

00:12:41.250 --> 00:12:45.180
we are from the investigations department 
and fight criminals in the field.

00:12:45.180 --> 00:12:46.570
This much is to be expected.

00:12:47.370 --> 00:12:49.080
<i>There she goes again, being condescending.</i>

00:12:49.460 --> 00:12:50.830
Please dodge that.

00:12:50.830 --> 00:12:51.850
What?

00:12:51.850 --> 00:12:53.110
Chuta, behind you!

00:12:53.110 --> 00:12:53.620
Huh?

00:12:54.880 --> 00:12:56.010
Ow.

00:12:57.410 --> 00:12:59.920
H-Hey! What was that for?!

00:12:59.920 --> 00:13:01.630
I told you to dodge.

00:13:01.630 --> 00:13:02.430
Wha—

00:13:02.830 --> 00:13:06.490
So if I told you to dodge, 
you'd dodge whatever?

00:13:06.490 --> 00:13:08.600
Yes. Even if you said, 
"Please dodge," or "Dodge that."

00:13:08.600 --> 00:13:10.770
Even if it was shortened to something 
like "dog," I'd dodge.

00:13:10.770 --> 00:13:13.970
"Dog"? That doesn't even 
mean the same thing!

00:13:15.440 --> 00:13:20.480
Dodge... doge... dog... 
"dodge" becomes "dog"!

00:13:21.410 --> 00:13:23.350
Misuzu is being ridiculous.

00:13:23.350 --> 00:13:24.570
Yeah.

00:13:24.570 --> 00:13:27.070
Th-Th-Th-Th-There's trouble, chu!

00:13:27.070 --> 00:13:29.950
It looks like level 100 
was somehow pushed, chu!

00:13:29.950 --> 00:13:32.480
Huh? Level 100?

00:13:36.330 --> 00:13:37.990
It looks like smoke.

00:13:37.990 --> 00:13:40.160
If we get stung by that many, 
we're going to die!

00:13:40.160 --> 00:13:42.540
Inspector Chips, please push the 
emergency stop button.

00:13:42.540 --> 00:13:44.880
I've been pushing it, 
but it's not working, chu!

00:13:44.880 --> 00:13:46.630
What?!

00:13:47.360 --> 00:13:51.840
Oh, there you are. I brought a 
notification about the bazaar.

00:13:52.360 --> 00:13:55.470
This isn't good, chu! 
Tonto's become the target!

00:13:56.960 --> 00:13:58.030
Flies?

00:14:02.370 --> 00:14:03.390
Meow!

00:14:04.980 --> 00:14:08.030
What is this? It's so fun!

00:14:08.030 --> 00:14:09.210
Huh?

00:14:12.200 --> 00:14:17.740
Annihilated! I'm an expert 
when it comes to fly swatting.

00:14:18.380 --> 00:14:20.850
I guess people have all kinds of talents.

00:14:24.870 --> 00:14:28.120
Since we actually fight criminals 
in the investigtions department,

00:14:28.120 --> 00:14:29.470
I guess we need to work harder...

00:14:30.090 --> 00:14:32.390
I shouldn't have told you to dodge earlier.

00:14:32.390 --> 00:14:33.480
Wha...

00:14:36.140 --> 00:14:38.350
<b>Bird Watching</b>

00:14:36.550 --> 00:14:38.340
<i>Have to keep an eye on 
the two transfer students.</i>

00:14:38.550 --> 00:14:40.300
<i>Have to keep an eye on 
the two transfer students.</i>

00:14:42.360 --> 00:14:44.950
Sonokata! Don't scare me like that!

00:14:44.950 --> 00:14:46.020
What is this?

00:14:46.020 --> 00:14:49.960
I-I thought it might be useful to keep 
an eye on the transfer students from far away.

00:14:49.960 --> 00:14:51.550
It actually makes you look 
even more suspicious.

00:14:51.550 --> 00:14:53.600
That's why it says "bird watching"!

00:14:53.600 --> 00:14:54.700
That's pointless.

00:14:56.710 --> 00:14:58.110
I told you, Dolugh.

00:14:58.110 --> 00:15:00.210
But you were going along with it, Chuta.

00:15:00.210 --> 00:15:02.100
<i>This is Inspector Chips, chu.</i>

00:15:02.100 --> 00:15:03.460
<i>Can you hear me, chu?</i>

00:15:03.460 --> 00:15:04.350
Yes.

00:15:04.350 --> 00:15:07.500
<i>The two transfer students have a cold and 
didn't come to school today, chu.</i>

00:15:08.190 --> 00:15:09.140
Cold?

00:15:10.670 --> 00:15:12.700
That's disappointing, Chuta.

00:15:12.700 --> 00:15:15.720
I guess the transfer students might not 
have had anything to do with it, after all.

00:15:15.720 --> 00:15:19.930
But isn't it weird that they both 
got a cold at the same time?

00:15:21.100 --> 00:15:26.450
This is sudden, but we've got 
a new transfer student in class today.

00:15:26.770 --> 00:15:29.390
N-Now there's one in our class?

00:15:27.040 --> 00:15:28.750
What? You didn't tell us!

00:15:29.390 --> 00:15:31.470
I guess things like this happen.

00:15:31.470 --> 00:15:32.610
Come on in.

00:15:41.730 --> 00:15:44.110
<i>G-Gucchi...?</i>

00:15:49.880 --> 00:15:54.970
<b>Fourth Generation Monitalien Water Planet Support-Type</b>

00:15:49.880 --> 00:15:54.970
<b>Dolughbritt Type 390</b>

00:15:55.430 --> 00:15:57.840
Go ahead and introduce yourself.

00:15:57.840 --> 00:16:00.650
What's wrong, Chuta? Your heart is racing.

00:16:01.350 --> 00:16:03.930
<i>He looks like Gucchi...</i>

00:16:03.930 --> 00:16:06.760
Nice to meet you all. I'm Mikio Narita.

00:16:03.940 --> 00:16:06.770
<b>Mikio Narita</b>

00:16:07.220 --> 00:16:10.630
<i>It's someone else? Well, of course, it is...</i>

00:16:12.560 --> 00:16:16.820
It looks like the school had no plans to accept 
a transfer student until this morning, chu.

00:16:16.820 --> 00:16:20.040
Also, there are no files 
on a Mikio Narita, chu.

00:16:20.040 --> 00:16:22.830
Just in case, keep an eye on 
that transfer student, chu.

00:16:22.830 --> 00:16:24.330
Yoyosa!

00:16:25.330 --> 00:16:29.660
He was in the reception room then.

00:16:29.660 --> 00:16:36.590
"He" means "he." "Then" means "then." 
"He" was in the reception room "then."

00:16:31.900 --> 00:16:35.230
So far, there is nothing suspicious 
about the transfer student.

00:16:35.230 --> 00:16:36.590
Roger, chu.

00:16:50.880 --> 00:16:53.400
Are you sure it's okay to approach 
him in the open like this?

00:16:53.400 --> 00:16:56.900
Talking to a classmate isn't weird, is it?

00:16:58.080 --> 00:16:58.570
Hey.

00:17:00.970 --> 00:17:03.170
I'm Kokonose. I'm in the same class as you.

00:17:03.170 --> 00:17:04.360
Hey.

00:17:04.360 --> 00:17:05.560
Are you heading home?

00:17:05.560 --> 00:17:07.840
I have to leave early 
because of my parents.

00:17:07.840 --> 00:17:11.120
Um... to some place called 
Keiki Town 8-chome.

00:17:11.850 --> 00:17:14.070
That's an address where Gucchi used to live!

00:17:14.950 --> 00:17:17.740
<i>What... What's with this guy?</i>

00:17:18.420 --> 00:17:23.010
I-I'm leaving early, too. I'm going 
the same way, so I'll show you the way.

00:17:23.010 --> 00:17:27.760
Huh? Nah, I'd feel bad. I have 
somewhere to stop along the way, too.

00:17:28.740 --> 00:17:30.490
Oh, that's fine.

00:17:32.100 --> 00:17:36.820
Inspector Chips, Officer Kokonose is tracking 
the transfer student and leaving school early.

00:17:36.820 --> 00:17:40.660
Roger, chu. Then I'll follow 
both of them, chu.

00:17:42.290 --> 00:17:46.940
Chief Laine! Headquarters have sent us 
data on the crew on the DeMillle ship.

00:17:46.940 --> 00:17:48.320
All right. Let's see it.

00:17:50.760 --> 00:17:52.940
<i>This face... I've seen it before.</i>

00:17:53.380 --> 00:17:58.420
Riggs, could you send me the 
case file on Case BD2382?

00:17:58.420 --> 00:17:59.510
Yoyosa!

00:17:59.510 --> 00:18:01.910
Harry, could you confirm 
if there's a possibility

00:18:01.910 --> 00:18:04.430
that the two I'm about to send you 
are the same person?

00:18:04.430 --> 00:18:05.800
Yoyosa!

00:18:06.260 --> 00:18:09.190
Inputting all of the data on the two.

00:18:09.190 --> 00:18:12.390
Using the truffle style algorithm 
to find the answer.

00:18:12.840 --> 00:18:14.150
We got results!

00:18:14.150 --> 00:18:17.790
There is a 98% probability that 
they are the same person.

00:18:17.790 --> 00:18:19.440
<i>I knew it...</i>

00:18:19.780 --> 00:18:21.160
How is Chuta doing?

00:18:21.160 --> 00:18:23.950
Um... Whoa, what is this?

00:18:23.950 --> 00:18:26.560
Various radars as well as 
communicators are down.

00:18:26.560 --> 00:18:27.960
It's due to outside interference.

00:18:27.960 --> 00:18:28.700
What?

00:18:28.700 --> 00:18:32.230
We're being hit by hardcore jamming! 
Communication with Earth is impossible.

00:18:32.230 --> 00:18:35.000
Locating the investigation personnel is impossible.

00:18:38.910 --> 00:18:42.300
The two have currently gone through 
a park and are heading north.

00:18:43.690 --> 00:18:45.260
Did you need something, chu?

00:18:45.260 --> 00:18:46.490
Yeah.

00:18:46.490 --> 00:18:48.560
We do, ēlDLIVE.

00:18:49.070 --> 00:18:51.220
Who are you, chu?

00:18:51.220 --> 00:18:53.350
You don't need to know that.

00:18:53.750 --> 00:18:55.950
Don't underestimate me, chu.

00:18:55.950 --> 00:19:02.880
This Melpleian humanoid powered armor 
has a number of SPH weapons equipped, chu.

00:19:06.030 --> 00:19:09.360
Guess you're about to find out 
personally, chu.

00:19:09.360 --> 00:19:12.830
Program drive, chu!

00:19:19.750 --> 00:19:26.480
Crap, chu! I pushed the 
emergency eject button, chu!

00:19:26.990 --> 00:19:28.340
Inspector Chips?

00:19:28.340 --> 00:19:30.900
<i>I can't eat another bite, chu...</i>

00:19:30.900 --> 00:19:31.640
<i>He fell asleep?</i>

00:19:32.990 --> 00:19:33.930
Misuzu?

00:19:33.940 --> 00:19:38.140
I left my racket on the court during 
morning practice, so I'm going to go get it.

00:19:38.480 --> 00:19:40.450
What? Right now?

00:19:41.660 --> 00:19:45.290
Inspector Chips! Officer Kokonose! 
Please come in!

00:19:48.120 --> 00:19:49.780
The jamming is intensifying!

00:19:49.780 --> 00:19:51.410
Hurry up with the analysis!

00:19:51.410 --> 00:19:52.630
Yoyosa!

00:19:52.630 --> 00:19:57.080
Even if we can't use the electromagnetic radar, 
the SPH radar should be functional.

00:19:57.080 --> 00:19:57.960
Méliès!

00:19:57.960 --> 00:19:59.380
Find Chuta and the others!

00:19:59.380 --> 00:20:00.790
Yoyosa!

00:20:03.020 --> 00:20:04.710
I'm unable to find even a faint trace

00:20:04.710 --> 00:20:07.560
of their SPH within a five-kilometer 
radius of the school.

00:20:07.560 --> 00:20:11.670
But it's possible they are actually in the vicinity.

00:20:11.980 --> 00:20:13.810
Because looking at the records 
from this morning,

00:20:13.810 --> 00:20:17.860
only the SPH signals from 
Chips, Misuzu, and Chuta are missing.

00:20:18.230 --> 00:20:23.150
Which means that something's blocking 
their specific SPHs from showing up on the radar.

00:20:23.150 --> 00:20:24.810
Something's...

00:20:24.810 --> 00:20:25.860
...not letting us track them?

00:20:29.600 --> 00:20:35.890
The Earth is being exposed to the jamming 
as well as to the SPH suppression rays.

00:20:35.890 --> 00:20:39.260
Ha ha! How do you like 
DeMille's newest weapon?

00:20:40.580 --> 00:20:43.380
ēlDLIVE must be in sheer panic right now.

00:20:43.380 --> 00:20:45.750
The captain can do 
all the bad things he wants.

00:20:46.480 --> 00:20:50.830
<i>This isn't good... Chuta and 
the others are isolated.</i>

00:20:53.390 --> 00:20:58.340
I-I'm surprised you needed 
to visit Sengen Shrine.

00:21:00.510 --> 00:21:02.970
So what did you need to do?

00:21:02.970 --> 00:21:04.650
It's nostalgic, isn't it?

00:21:05.380 --> 00:21:07.490
We used to play here all the time...

00:21:07.820 --> 00:21:09.410
...with Michiyo and Matsutaro.

00:21:14.580 --> 00:21:15.980
Inspector Chips!

00:21:17.080 --> 00:21:18.730
Please wake up!

00:21:21.150 --> 00:21:24.210
Your scent is irresistible...

00:21:24.210 --> 00:21:25.750
Sonokata Misuzu.

00:21:25.750 --> 00:21:27.080
The transfer students!

00:21:27.610 --> 00:21:29.000
Nap time.

00:21:40.110 --> 00:21:45.380
We all fell off a cliff and died, so why 
were you the only one allowed to survive,

00:21:47.170 --> 00:21:48.570
Chuta?

00:21:49.480 --> 00:21:53.020
So you really are Gucchi!

00:23:25.700 --> 00:23:29.530
Sonokata looked just like her mom! 
They had the same eyes.

00:23:29.530 --> 00:23:32.780
At this rate, I guess that's how 
Sonokata's going to look, too...

00:23:32.780 --> 00:23:33.980
Uh... Right.

00:23:33.980 --> 00:23:35.280
Next time on <i>ēlDLIVE,</i>

00:23:35.100 --> 00:23:39.970
<b>Next Time
A Pursuer From the Past: Part 2</b>

00:23:35.280 --> 00:23:37.290
"A Pursuer From the Past: Part 2."

00:23:37.290 --> 00:23:40.020
Isn't DNA amazing, Chuta?!
